==German==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|trucken}}, {{m|gmh|trocken}}, from {{inh|de|goh|truckan}}, {{m|goh|trokkan||dried out, parched, thirsty, dry}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*druknaz}}, {{m|gem-pro|*druhnaz||dry}}, from {{der|de|ine-pro|*dʰerǵʰ-||to strengthen; become hard or solid}}, from {{m|ine-pro|*dʰer-||to hold, hold fast, support}}. The form ''trucken'' was originally predominant, but the word eventually became standardized in an old western variant with ''-o-''. Cognate with {{cog|osx|drokno||dry|pos=adverb}}, {{cog|ang|ġedrycnan||to dry up}}.

